# D27 accept-both, SELF-HOST resolver lane: the canonical `^` move sigil as an
# UNNAMED FUNCTION-TYPE PARAMETER SUFFIX (`Callable[void(int &, String ^)]`) —
# the D35 spelling, sigil AFTER the type.
#
# AXIS CELL: glyph = `^` · position = fn-type unnamed-param suffix · callee
# shape = PARAMETER-passed callable · lanes = Rust gg (C + LLVM), self-host
# resolver, self-host runtime.
#
# `!` CONTROL: `callable_bang_arr_indexed_callee.gg:27` is the ONLY in-corpus
# postfix-`!` twin of this position and is the accept-both control for this
# cell — same two-parameter `&`/move pair in the fn type, differing in the
# glyph. No new `!` site is added (`fmt_no_new_move_bang_in_migrated_corpora`
# in tests/lints.rs is shrink-only and at zero headroom).
#
# ⚠ The callee shape is load-bearing, not incidental. TWO shapes were
# measured and rejected for this cell:
#   - Callable-typed LOCAL VARIABLE (`Callable[...] f = mix; f(&a, ^s)`) —
#     ICEs the Rust lowerer ("Tier 2a consume-site violation",
#     src/ir/lowering/mod.rs:2114) for BOTH glyphs identically. Pre-existing
#     and glyph-independent; repro at
#     known_gaps/callable_local_var_consuming_arg_ices.gg.
#   - INDEXED callee out of a Vector (`arr[0](&a, ^s)`) — runs on Rust gg but
#     TIMES OUT on the self-host runtime lane. Its `!` twin
#     `callable_bang_arr_indexed_callee.gg` has no committed snapshot either,
#     i.e. that shape has NEVER matched on the self-host lane. Also
#     pre-existing and glyph-independent.
# The parameter-passed shape below exercises the SAME parse predicate and
# runs on every lane, so this cell pins D27 rather than either of those
# unrelated defects.
#
# RED-verified against the PRE-port self-host resolver driver: the fn-type
# param-suffix predicate accepted only the retired glyph, so the `^` was not
# consumed as an ownership marker and the type parse desynchronized.
# Post-port the resolver output matches Rust gg's.
#
# Expected stdout: hi\n101

void mix(int &n, String ^s):
    n = n + 100
    print(s)

void apply(Callable[void(int &, String ^)] cb, int &a, String ^s):
    cb(&a, ^s)

void main():
    int a = 1
    String greeting = "hi"
    apply(mix, &a, ^greeting)
    print(a)
